NUCLEO-F303RE
=============

An STM32F303RE: a Cortex-M4 with 512K of flash, 64K of SRAM and 16K of
core coupled memory, and a floating point extension that is single
precision only.

This kernel does not fit, and this is what that means in numbers.

What was measured
-----------------

Linked with the configuration beside this file, which is the smallest
one that still links -- no root file system, no Limbo, no ip, no ssl, no
capabilities, no profiling:

	text	259416	  flash is 524288, so this fits
	data	 50368
	bss	 38560
		------
		 88928	  RAM is 81920, so this does not

That is before any heap at all.  Inferno wants hundreds of kilobytes of
heap to load a Dis module into, and there is none left.

The second wall
---------------

Even with the memory, the floating point would not work.  The Cortex-M4
has FPv4-SP, which has no double precision instructions, and
utils/tl/thumb.c gives every F register a D register -- the way the FPA
it replaces held one value whatever the memory format was.  Linking with

	tl -M -F ...

names every function that would fault: the Dis interpreter's real
arithmetic, its conversions, and everything in libmath.  A Cortex-M4
needs software double precision before it can run any of this, either as
calls the linker emits or as emulation from the fault, which is what
os/inferno/port/fpiarm.c did for the FPA on ARM.

What is here anyway
-------------------

The board itself: the clock tree taken to 64MHz off the internal
oscillator with the flash wait states and the APB1 divider that go with
it, and the USART the ST-LINK's virtual serial port is wired to on PA2
and PA3.  None of it has been run.  It is written from RM0316 and the
NUCLEO-64 schematic, and it is the part that a Cortex-M4 with more
memory -- an STM32F4 or F7 -- would want, since those differ from this
in their memory and their peripherals and not in their core.

What would have to change
-------------------------

Software double precision, and a board with at least a quarter of a
megabyte of RAM.  Neither is a change to this directory.
